.TH TOMESH 1
.SH NAME
tomesh \- write the triangles of parts as an OBJ mesh
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tomesh
[
.B \-c
.I chord
] [
.B \-a
.I deg
] [
.B \-n
]
.IR part.fold | stream | \-
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Tomesh
writes each part of a fold file, or each solid of a stream,
as an object of a Wavefront OBJ file on the standard output:
.PP
.RS
.nf
o NAME
# colour R G B
v X Y Z
vn X Y Z
f A B C
.fi
.RE
.PP
The colour is that of a placed part, from 0 to 1.
Vertices are in world mm, numbered from 1 through the file;
triangles are counterclockwise seen from outside.
Each mesh is closed (faces share the points of their edges).
.TP
.BI \-c " chord"
Keep every triangle within
.I chord
mm of its face (default 0.02).
.TP
.BI \-a " deg"
Let no triangle turn more than
.I deg
degrees (default 10).
.TP
.B \-n
Write vertex normals, with faces as
.IB a // n .
.SH SEE ALSO
fold(5), part(5), view(1)
